{
  "dom_id": "step-q341794",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "$$\nf(x)\u223c\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=3{x}^{2}+4x$ for $x\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ The Fourier series of the $\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $f(x)=3{x}^{2}+4x$ for $x\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(3{x}^{2}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}]}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }((\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{8}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2})-(-\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{8}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
